From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fingerprint Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: size the reference retry to the measured blackout

The blackout has a clear onset. An identification completed at 14:27:50.685,
ending through the finger-up sub-SSM and its sleep:

  Manual FDT finger-up confirmed after 7 polls
  GOODIX_FINGER_UP_NUM_STATES entering state 3    (sleep)
  Device reported identify completion

The next action started about two seconds later and read empty reference
frames from 14:27:53 until 14:28:04, then recovered on its own and stayed
healthy for the rest of the session, including two full enrolments and a match
scoring 6448582.

So the sensor stops producing frames after an action that ends in sleep, and
comes back after roughly eleven seconds. The retry added with the reference
check was sized at eight attempts a tenth of a second apart, about one second,
which is an order of magnitude short of that: seventeen empty frames were
caught but five actions still failed with the budget spent.

Cover the measured recovery instead. Sixty attempts a quarter of a second
apart is about fifteen seconds, so a blackout becomes a wait rather than a
refusal. Waiting is the right trade for an authenticator, because the
alternative is turning away an operator who did nothing wrong.

This absorbs the fault rather than curing it. Why the sensor stops answering
after a sleep is still unknown, and three explanations for it have now been
measured and discarded: the sleep command alone (the open sequence ends with
the same command and the next action is fine), reinitialisation afterwards
(it re-runs the whole open including the USB reset and the frames stay empty),
and read desynchronisation (the reply framing across the boundary is
byte-for-byte that of a healthy read).

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
@@ -105,11 +105,18 @@
 /* The no-finger reference frame is subtracted from every capture, so one that
  * carries no signal silently changes the preprocessing rather than failing.
  * Healthy frames average about 2350 here; frames read while the sensor had
- * stopped responding average 0 to 10. The condition clears by itself, so a
- * bounded retry recovers without failing the operator's action. */
+ * stopped responding average 0 to 10.
+ *
+ * The condition follows an action that ended in sleep and clears by itself.
+ * One measured blackout ran from 14:27:53 to 14:28:04, so the budget covers
+ * about fifteen seconds: the first attempt at this used eight retries a tenth
+ * of a second apart, roughly one second, and five actions failed inside a
+ * blackout eleven times longer than the budget meant to absorb it. Waiting is
+ * the right trade here, because the alternative is refusing an operator who
+ * did nothing wrong. */
 #define GOODIX_REFERENCE_MIN_MEAN 200
-#define GOODIX_REFERENCE_MAX_RETRIES 8
-#define GOODIX_REFERENCE_RETRY_DELAY_MS 120
+#define GOODIX_REFERENCE_MAX_RETRIES 60
+#define GOODIX_REFERENCE_RETRY_DELAY_MS 250
 
 /* PSK white box for writing all-zero PSK */
 #define GOODIX_PSK_WHITE_BOX_LEN 96

